Yes. It is still one secret for you to manage, and both smtprelay and
mbsync read it the same way. The spec is posted as "[PATCH v7]
jails/instances/lab-mail: Initial spec" [1].

v7 stores the login and app password in one file,
/jails/data/lab-mail/secrets/creds, as one line: the login, one
space, and the app password. The login is an email address and has no
space in it, so the line splits at the first space, and the password
is the rest of the line whatever it contains. Alternatives considered
now records the login in the repo config as the rejected choice.
Nothing else changed; the interdiff against v6 is under the "---".

I will post the implementation once you accept the spec.

